From: Cindy Krafft <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:46:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix smooth_knn_dist giving sigma = inf for points with a
 disconnected neighbour

Neighbours pruned by disconnection_distance (and inf entries of a
precomputed distance matrix) reach smooth_knn_dist as knn_dists = inf. The
MIN_K_DIST_SCALE floor was computed from np.mean(ith_distances), which is
inf for such rows, so the floor replaced the searched sigma with inf and
compute_membership_strengths then gave every remaining edge of the point a
membership strength of exactly 1.0. The global mean_distances was inf as
well as soon as any row contained an inf, which did the same to every row
with rho == 0.

Exclude non-finite distances from rho and from both means. Rows without a
pruned neighbour are unchanged. Adds a unit test on smooth_knn_dist and a
UMAP-level test with disconnection_distance on the exact and the
approximate nearest-neighbour paths.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
